Let $L$ be a holomorphic line bundle on a connected Riemann surface $C$. Suppose that $a_\bullet:L\to[0,\infty)$ is finite, plurisubharmonic, and not identically zero, and that its restriction to every fiber is a Hermitian positive semidefinite quadratic form. In a nonvanishing holomorphic frame $e$ on $U\subset C$, write $$a_\bullet(z,w e(z))=u_e(z)|w|^2.$$ Then $\log u_e$, with the value $-\infty$ allowed, is subharmonic and locally integrable. The local measures $i\partial\bar\partial\log u_e$ define a positive Radon measure $\mu$ on $C$.*


*If a holomorphic bundle automorphism $\widetilde T:L\to L$ covers an automorphism $T:C\to C$ and satisfies $a_\bullet\circ\widetilde T=a_\bullet$, then $T^*\mu=\mu$. If $C=\mathbb P^1$ and $L=\mathcal O_{\mathbb P^1}(-b)$ with $b\geq1$, then $$\label{eq:seminorm-curvature-mass}
 \mu(\mathbb P^1)=2\pi b.$$
